From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: gregordinary <33880035+gregordinary@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 27 Jul 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] accel/rocket: make the RK3576 completion poll period tunable

PC_DONE is read-only in INTERRUPT_MASK on RK3576, so it cannot be routed
to the GIC and the driver polls it on an hrtimer instead of taking a
completion interrupt.  The period is hardcoded at 1 ms, and because a
submit cannot complete faster than one poll, that period IS the
per-submit floor on this SoC: every cost table for this part is a
submit-count table because of it.

Measured on an H96 MAX M9 by the wall time of a one-task 8x8 int8
convolution, five repetitions per point:

  poll period   1000us  500us  250us  200us  150us  100us
  per-submit     1.2ms  0.65ms 0.45ms 0.40ms 0.32ms wedges

The floor tracks the period one for one down to about 150 us, where
roughly 0.15 ms of non-poll cost is left (the ioctl round trips, the job
setup, the completion readback).  So the stock 1 ms is worth 3.75x on
every submit-bound workload, and on a part whose dispatch floor dominates
its cost model that is the single largest lever the driver holds.

It is a parameter rather than a shorter default because the two failures
below it are not understood:

  - At 100 us the IOMMU wedges with "Enable stall request timed out",
    and every later submit times out with its output buffer untouched.
    Whether that is the poll rate or the stale-page-fault clear not
    covering a job that completes this fast is not decoded.

  - At 200 us a convolution workload is unaffected (102 gate shapes
    bit-exact, no dmesg) while a matmul workload that drives the DPU's
    32-bit output writer starts failing.  That path already carries a
    known hazard whose clear is a runtime-PM power cycle, and the
    interaction between the two has not been separated.

Default 1000, so behaviour is unchanged unless the period is set.  RK3588
does not poll at all and is untouched.

Signed-off-by: gregordinary <33880035+gregordinary@users.noreply.github.com>
---
--- a/drivers/accel/rocket/rocket_job.c
+++ b/drivers/accel/rocket/rocket_job.c
@@ -29,7 +29,21 @@
  */
 #define PC_INTERRUPT_MASK_RK3576_PC_DONE_0  0x10000000u
 #define PC_INTERRUPT_MASK_RK3576_PC_DONE_1  0x20000000u
-#define RK3576_POLL_INTERVAL_NS  1000000LL  /* 1 ms */
+#define RK3576_POLL_INTERVAL_US_DEFAULT  1000u  /* 1 ms */
+
+static unsigned int rocket_poll_interval_us = RK3576_POLL_INTERVAL_US_DEFAULT;
+module_param_named(poll_interval_us, rocket_poll_interval_us, uint, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(poll_interval_us,
+		 "RK3576 PC_DONE completion poll period, in microseconds (default 1000)");
+
+static inline ktime_t rocket_poll_period(void)
+{
+	unsigned int us = READ_ONCE(rocket_poll_interval_us);
+
+	if (!us)
+		us = 1;
+	return ns_to_ktime((s64)us * NSEC_PER_USEC);
+}
 
 /*
  * PC_TASK_CON packs TASK_NUMBER in the low bits with the control bits directly
@@ -191,7 +205,7 @@
 
 	if (core->soc->poll_completion) {
 		atomic_set(&core->poll_active, 1);
-		hrtimer_start(&core->poll_timer, ns_to_ktime(RK3576_POLL_INTERVAL_NS),
+		hrtimer_start(&core->poll_timer, rocket_poll_period(),
 			      HRTIMER_MODE_REL);
 	} else {
 		dev_dbg(core->dev, "Submitted regcmd at 0x%llx to core %d",
@@ -395,7 +409,7 @@
 		return HRTIMER_NORESTART;
 	}
 
-	hrtimer_forward_now(timer, ns_to_ktime(RK3576_POLL_INTERVAL_NS));
+	hrtimer_forward_now(timer, rocket_poll_period());
 	return HRTIMER_RESTART;
 }
 
